(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ec-easy-2026-006"]={"v":1,"id":"ec-easy-2026-006","title":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","code":"EC","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering","seriesId":"ec-easy-2026","num":6,"category":"basic","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering"},"source":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Electronics_Engineering/012_Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>There are four types of candidates in an institute preparing for the UPSC. The number of students of Engineering, Science, Commerce and Humanities is 40, 60, 50 and 30 respectively and the respective percentage of students who qualified the UPSC is 80%, 75%, 60% and 50% respectively. The overall percentage of successful candidates in the institute is :</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"67.77%"},{"key":"B","html":"66.66%"},{"key":"C","html":"68.5%"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c572b8fd90262ce8f19.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The number 12375 is divisible by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3"},{"key":"B","html":"9"},{"key":"C","html":"11"},{"key":"D","html":"7"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)<br />\n&bull; For a number to be divisible by 3 and 9, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 3 and 9<br />\nrespectively. Here, 1 + 2 + 3 + 7 + 5 = 18, which is divisible 3 and 9 both. Hence, the number is<br />\ndivisible by both 3 and 9.<br />\n&bull; For a number to be divisible by 11, the difference between the sum of digits in the odd<br />\npositions and even positions must be a multiple of 11 or 0. Here, (5 + 3 + 1) &ndash; (7 + 2) = 0. Hence,<br />\nthe number is divisible by 11.</p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Number of even divisor of 5400.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"36"},{"key":"B","html":"48"},{"key":"C","html":"24"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8f9036f2a4ceb7354851.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the given figure, ∠BAC and ∠BDC are the angles of same segments, ∠DBC = 30° and ∠BCD = 110°. ∠BAC is equal to </p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02ea2b22bdc24ebceafe.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"35°"},{"key":"B","html":"40°"},{"key":"C","html":"55°"},{"key":"D","html":"60°"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99691760b9c1b028cee8.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Sum of all numbers n such that n! ends with 30 zeros.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"610"},{"key":"B","html":"590"},{"key":"C","html":"614"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n124! ends with 28 zeros and 125! ends with 31 zeros.<br />\nTherefore, there is no integer n with n! ending in exactly 30 zeros.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/4689da9997b68e26e68b.png\" /></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/45d977661fe05c55d7f1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the diagram given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e883276e1f9f9bc336c0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Five hundred candidates appeared in an examination comprising of tests in English, Hindi and Mathematics. The diagram gives the number of candidates who failed in different tests. The percentage of candidates who failed in at least two subjects is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.078"},{"key":"B","html":"1.0"},{"key":"C","html":"6.8"},{"key":"D","html":"7.8"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/826992f2a1fec813a92a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the mirror represented by a line <em>MN</em>, choose the correct mirror-image of the figure, from amongst the four alternatives (a), (b), (c) and (d) given along with it.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f6828b0238a54662e652.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a9/a9b437bc1a19241d37e8.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/9454f4883848a05d37ce.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3371ce9b448e4723409.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2dc1f7c540fb97d32bf4.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Read the passage carefully and choose the best answer to the following question from the four alternatives given below.<br />\nAmong the natural resources which can be called upon in national plan for development, possibly<br />\nthe most important is human labour; without productive labour force, including effective leadership<br />\nand intelligent middle management, no amount of foreign assistance or natural wealth can ensure<br />\nsuccessful development and modernisation. One essential factor is usually overlooked or ignored.<br />\nThe forgotten factor is the role of women. Development will be handicapped as long as women<br />\nremain second-class citizens, uneducated, without any voice in family or community decisions,<br />\nwithout legal or economic status, married when they are still practically children, and thenceforth<br />\nproducing one baby after another, often only to see half of them die before they are of school age.<br />\nWe can enhance development by improving ‘woman power’ by giving women opportunity to develop themselves.<br />\nThe most important natural resource for national development is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"human labour"},{"key":"B","html":"effective leadership"},{"key":"C","html":"intelligent middle management"},{"key":"D","html":"foreign assistance"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nThe passage clearly states that among natural resources, human labour is the most important for national development.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the following question, a part of the sentence is given in bold. Choose the correct alternative that best improves the bold part. If no improvement is needed, select “No improvement.”<br />\nHe likes to drive his car at a speed of eighty kilometres <strong>each hour.</strong></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"in every hour"},{"key":"B","html":"an hour"},{"key":"C","html":"hourly"},{"key":"D","html":"No improvement"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nThe correct expression is &ldquo;eighty kilometres an hour&rdquo; (or per hour). The word &ldquo;each&rdquo; is<br />\ngrammatically incorrect in this context. &ldquo;Correct sentence: &ldquo;He likes to drive his car at a speed of<br />\neighty kilometres an hour.&rdquo;</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Duality of DFT is expressed as</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7074d32b08d04eb00bb.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7031089867df1a1a286.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e800e06b530aca7132a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6f4d2e9fe894ef59dc60.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a3a4bffc1ea20f6f9b7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For an AM signal, what is the modulation percentage if the amplitude of sinusoidal modulating signal is 8 V and that of carrier is 12 V?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"50"},{"key":"B","html":"67"},{"key":"C","html":"150"},{"key":"D","html":"33"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/829fbc899dfe26a85c37.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the system shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/469510fde448e11f3894.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>This system is stable for</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8dcb735a5bb9061bc877.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"0 < <em>K</em> < 20"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc88168243e0a6e8650c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>K</em> > 20"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/94d37042e66de7de1097.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The range of numbers that can be represented by 6-bit 2’s complement number is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"–31 to 31"},{"key":"B","html":"–32 to 31"},{"key":"C","html":"–63 to 63"},{"key":"D","html":"–64 to 63"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/fe070e367ace4c5034fc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Let <em>X</em>(<em>z</em>) be the Z-transform of a discrete time sequence <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] = (–2)<sup>–n</sup> <em>u</em>[<em>n</em>]. Consider another signal <em>y</em>[<em>n</em>] and its Z-transform is <em>Y</em>(z), given as Y(z) = X(z<sup>–2</sup>). Then the value of y[n] at n = –2 is _______.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-0.8,-0.3],"answerText":"-0.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-0.5 (-0.80 - -0.30)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cd/cd1312b85aa135426acf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/51/51d846d517ebb863fda3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/565ece2947cfa7bfec73.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The characteristic equation of the BJT can be given as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fbfaef132fe0e79eff63.png\" />If the transistor is<br />\nbiased with <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e5de79240ee47bdfa96.png\" /> = 3 mA, then the value of small signal output resistance, <em>r</em><sub>0</sub> is equal to ___________. (upto two decimal places)<br />\n(Assume no early effect and V<sub>T</sub> = 25 mV)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[10,15],"answerText":"12.34","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>12.34 (10.00 - 15.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a2/a28bbd4e00d1f345738e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":17,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>If an n-channel E-MOSFET has <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/662901925543ff72596e.png\" /> and the over drive voltage required to operate the MOSFET in saturation region is 4 V, then the drain current produced by the E-MOSFET is __________ mA. (upto 1 decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.8,4],"answerText":"3.2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.2 (2.8 - 4.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/34eb284922fec6a69eaf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The fermi potential of a <em>p</em>-type substrate of a MOS capacitor at equilibrium is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/11b902d5a018647a10ea.png\" /> What happens when surface potential equal to <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d909012448759b42dd48.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The majority carrier concentration at the surface equal to the majority carrier concentration in the bulk."},{"key":"B","html":"The minority carrier concentration at the surface equal to the intrinsic carrier concentration."},{"key":"C","html":"The minority carrier concentration at the surface equal to the majority carrier concentration in the bulk."},{"key":"D","html":"The minority carrier concentration at the surface equal to the minority carrier concentration in the bulk."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/026c1c914b05d6d5d55f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A transmission line filled with lossless dielectric has characteristic impedance of 50 Ω. If the capacitance per unit length is 0.10 nF/m, then relative dielectric constant of the dielectric is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.25"},{"key":"B","html":"5.06"},{"key":"C","html":"1.25"},{"key":"D","html":"1.5"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3483816a25eddbd2a01f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the derivation of expression for peak percent overshoot:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83fc451a183f0be121fa.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>which of the following conditions is not required?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"System is linear and time invariant."},{"key":"B","html":"The system transfer function has a pair of complex conjugate poles and no zeroes."},{"key":"C","html":"There is no transportation delay in the system."},{"key":"D","html":"The system has zero initial conditions."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff85c76973fd5b03e807.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>If A is a matrix such that <em>A</em><sup>2</sup> + <em>A</em> + 2<em>I</em> = 0, then which of the following is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A is non singular"},{"key":"B","html":"A is symmetric"},{"key":"C","html":"A cannot be skew-symmetric"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f00486bc1e5ef753326.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/750a772a75f6b7e1b8f4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A fair coin is tossed 100 times. The probability of getting tails 1, 3, _ _ _ _ _ 49 times is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e7/e70a6b7b99f6e7efaf30.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f0c26ff2e6ae3c54725d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/474abee971b781e5bbc1.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d3f52eb493d85187c81f.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16cfeab6147458730ce5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d269fd2b38e3f58063d8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the discrete memoryless channel shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26872a2e7bec5b3c3de5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The probabilities <em>P</em>(<em>x</em><sub>1</sub>) = 0.40 and <em>P</em>(<em>x</em><sub>0</sub>) = 0.60. If it is known that the transmitted symbol is <em>x</em><sub>1</sub>, then the average information that can be obtained by reading the corresponding output symbols is __________ bits/symbol. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.95,0.99],"answerText":"0.97","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.97 (0.95 - 0.99)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b47161d4b582ce871b2d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In a 9-stage ripple counter, the propagation delay of a flip-flop is 10 ns. If the pulse width of the strobe pulse is 15 ns, then the maximum frequency at which the counter will operate reliably is __________ MHz. (upto 1 decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9,10],"answerText":"9.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>9.5 (9.0 - 10.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f90d7ffdc9f92d31e839.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For an OP-amp having a slew rate of 3 V/μsec, what is the maximum closed loop voltage gain that can be used when the input signal varies by 0.4 V in 12 μsec?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"60"},{"key":"B","html":"30"},{"key":"C","html":"40"},{"key":"D","html":"90"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/444d1ba62addcfe9a5b6.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/151cd0744d85cad09bf2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Let the Fourier transform of a signal <em>x</em>(<em>t</em>) is represented as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b8d725f6f9f09e16994a.png\" /> then the value of <em>x</em>(<em>t</em>) at t = 0 will be _____________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0,0],"answerText":"0","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0 (0 - 0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a4698af348cd51648dfa.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/58093f28ad0972d8cd5c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The transistor has <em>g<sub>m</sub></em> = 2 mA/V and value of <em>R<sub>D</sub></em> and <em>R<sub>s</sub></em> is equal to 20 kΩ and 4 kΩ respectively.<br />\nThen the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01c2e361df3e715e0cab.png\" /> is equal to ___________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-6,-4],"answerText":"-5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-5 (-6 - -4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f33e1b45c5b1c5bcd404.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Let a memory chip is represented as 8192 × 64. If there are A number of address lines and <em>B </em>number of data lines in the chip, then <em>A</em> + <em>B</em> is __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[77,77],"answerText":"77","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>77 (77 - 77)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e46a1e36b59a10af6a2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Let <em>x</em>(<em>t</em>) be a signal with its Fourier transform <em>X</em>(<em>j</em>ω). Suppose we are given the following facts:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/809d82b37b3ec6e63197.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Then the closed form expression for <em>x</em>(<em>t</em>) is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9cf3112177dd4f88447b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cc716f234584942eeb93.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/60778ca41185856c3ac3.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f74d04c5dffe1cc3a1b.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f4ddd5281d9709f945e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/9888ec5b35d6fa3e6936.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A DSB-SC signal is generated by using the modulator shown below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/695bbd7522598b45059e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Here, <em>m</em>(<em>t</em>) is a message signal which is band-limited to <em>f<sub>m</sub></em>. The bandpass filter is ideal with a bandwidth of B centered around fc. The carrier generator generates cos<sup>3</sup>(2π f<sub>c</sub>t), but not cos(2π <em>f<sub>c</sub>t</em>).<br />\nIf <em>f<sub>c</sub></em> = 10 <em>f<sub>m</sub></em>, then for proper production of the DSB-SC signal with a carrier frequency of fc at the output, the condition to be satisfied is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6abd5fdd725a2ed6959d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/ad4bf8de67a43d417c15.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/856aeec6d2e4aa6aaeca.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/00a24458c83e092e194d.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4ce221c71437faa9957a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5a3ab498c8d1a6be52d7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The closed-loop transfer function of a system is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d58bd5d2464618371092.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>For this system, the maximum peak overshoot of the unit step response exists at</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff05c08fc96489f312d0.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c75173d2f887f2cfdbed.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e7/e7fe1be17e5afb0c28f5.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9e/9e6a105475fe2136c7de.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/094cbc1e229c5c199a91.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/adf1da86901e58b6dc89.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the voltage across <em>Z<sub>L</sub></em> is to be independent of the value of <em>Z<sub>L</sub></em>, then the value of <em>C</em> should be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.785 μF"},{"key":"B","html":"2.325 μF"},{"key":"C","html":"3.125 μF"},{"key":"D","html":"4.505 μF"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53f47535cb7ffe282966.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b35e39b60a281b1551b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If <img align=\"absmiddl\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/965eb520dc27fbddfa3c.png\" /> = 18sin(2t) A, then the voltage <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4a/4a78e84370fb34f9bf50.png\" /> across the 2 H inductor will be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10sin(2<em>t</em>) V"},{"key":"B","html":"12cos(2<em>t</em>) V"},{"key":"C","html":"15sin(2<em>t</em>) V"},{"key":"D","html":"18sin(2<em>t</em>) V"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec0c284769707a8bc47b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The samples of a message signal <em>X</em>(<em>t</em>) are applied to a 16-level uniform mid-rise quantizer. The peak and rms values of the message signal are x<sub>max</sub> and x<sub>rms</sub> respectively. The dynamic range of the quantizer is from –x<sub>max</sub> to +x<sub>max</sub>. The quantization error is uniformly distributed over <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/dbd274b13e30cd7deea0.png\" />where Δ is the uniform step-size. If the signal-to-quantization noise ratio at the output of the quantizer is 25 dB, then the value of the crest or peak factor <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d8854e169bd5904adfe.png\" />of the message signal is _________. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.4,1.7],"answerText":"1.56","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.56 (1.40 - 1.70)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e91cf47b8c1593f53bf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/5311f8761e420fa9dfc9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/20/20b55abcfe2a2cbfd404.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>Then <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is continuous at <em>x</em> = 4 when</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>a</em> = 0, <em>b</em> = 0"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>a</em> = 1, <em>b</em> = 1"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>a</em> = –1, <em>b</em> = 1"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>a</em> = 1, <em>b</em> = –1"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e0501654c26ecae6b16.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f5/f5922992de0f318592a8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":36,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The received signal is <em>r</em>(<em>t</em>) = <em>s</em>(<em>t</em>) + <em>n</em>(<em>t</em>) where <em>s</em>(<em>t</em>) is the signal and <em>n</em>(<em>t</em>) is the noise signal. The signal <em>s</em>(<em>t</em>) is a random process with an auto-correlation <em>R<sub>s</sub></em>(τ) = 5<sub>e</sub>–|τ|. The noise <em>n</em>(<em>t</em>) is a sample function of a random process with auto-correlation <em>R<sub>n</sub></em>(τ) = e<sup>–5</sup>|τ|. If the two processes are having zero mean value and are independent of each other, the total power of <em>r</em>(<em>t</em>) is _________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,7],"answerText":"6","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6 (5 - 7)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d7727d87e9af558339b6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The carrier concentration in an instrinsic semiconductor at 300 K is 1.5 × 10<sup>10</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>. If donor impurities are introduced with a concentration of 10<sup>18</sup> cm–3, then the new electron concentration per cm<sup>–3</sup> at 300 K will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3 × 10<sup>18</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"4 × 10<sup>18</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"1 × 10<sup>18</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"6 × 10<sup>18</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9e/9eaee1f8641e42ac63e6.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0ca37a6ac0ec6a9a0ae0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The number of 2 input NOR gates required to design a 4 bit even parity generator are ___________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[15,15],"answerText":"15","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>15 (15 - 15)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/8025c3e3cf3e83c4ae22.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18bfcc42e101db5d22d8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The circuit is a current amplifier with amplification factor <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/013a83bc34cf9e26f0c9.png\" /> If the op-amp is ideal, then the value of resistance <em>R</em> is equal to</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"500 Ω"},{"key":"B","html":"0.33 kΩ"},{"key":"C","html":"1.5 kΩ"},{"key":"D","html":"2 kΩ"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/10/10f94310182af65b0f5c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The Norton’s equivalent resistance across the terminals <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> for the circuit shown in the figure below is ________ Ω.</p>\n\n<p>(upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99226f76c0aa7699d326.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,3],"answerText":"2.72","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.72 (2.00 - 3.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/51/51c1cf971fdd7b71149b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/27/274f5f063428727e99dd.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the MOS transistor shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/867627f87ca476612a54.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Both transistors <em>M</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>M</em><sub>2</sub> have <em>V<sub>TN</sub></em> = 0.8 V and μ<sub>n</sub>C<sub>ox</sub> = 30 μA/V<sup>2</sup>. If the value of V<sub>0</sub> = 2.91 V, then the ratio of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa1dc2e460dc3d6eeb37.png\" /> is equal to ________ (upto 2 decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,3],"answerText":"2.67","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.67 (2.00 - 3.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/eff877588cba9b492ade.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the signal flow graph shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ad/ade40dc959c0993478cc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The gain <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c901e58023d0722dec63.png\" /> is equal to __________. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4.25,4.29],"answerText":"4.27","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.27 (4.25 - 4.29)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec3efe9cda20b7825524.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which one of the following statements is correct?<br />\nWhen an electromagnetic wave strikes the air dielectric interface at an angle,</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"the electromagnetic wave is diffracted."},{"key":"B","html":"the electromagnetic wave is reflected back according to Snell’s law."},{"key":"C","html":"the tangential magnetic flux density components are continuous."},{"key":"D","html":"the normal electric flux density components have same value."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f2083edaf2eb83517eb0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The output y[n] of a discrete time LTI system is found to be <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0b/0b5946532e7e624ca244.png\" /> when input <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] is u[n].<br />\nThe output y[n] is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/cd/cd1f855c024b6b0eec38.png\" /> Then the value of (<em>k</em><sub>1</sub> + <em>k</em><sub>2</sub>)<br />\nis __________</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cb72838311416faea557.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":45,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A zero mean white Gaussian random process <em>X</em>(<em>t</em>) is passed through an LTI system whose impulse response <em>h</em>(<em>t</em>) is shown below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3e/3ecbede66049b4727db1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the two-sided PSD of the input process <em>X</em>(<em>t</em>) is 3 W/Hz, then the variance of the output process of the system will be ____________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19f1c1a51720339daa6a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A code is said to be self-complementing, if the code word of 9’s complement <em>N</em> can be obtained by the 1’s complement of the code word of N."},{"key":"B","html":"Cyclic codes generally have unit distance between two consecutive codes."},{"key":"C","html":"4221 and 5211 are examples of sequential codes."},{"key":"D","html":"Adding a parity bit can also detect position of a single bit error."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)<br />\n&bull; A code is said to be self - complementing, if code word of the 9&rsquo;s complement of N [i.e (9-N)]<br />\ncan be obtained from the code word of N by interchanging 0&rsquo;s and 1&rsquo;s i.e. by taking the 1&rsquo;s<br />\ncomplement of the code word of N.<br />\n&bull; A cyclic code is a block code, where the circular shifts of each codeword gives another word<br />\nthat belongs to the code. Thus, they generally have unit distance between two consecutive<br />\ncodes.<br />\n&bull; In sequential codes, each succeeding code is one binary number greater than its preceding<br />\ncode. 4221 and 5211 binary codes are as given below:</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d70a6417f2844e303c8d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The area enclosed between the curves <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/66aed5316424b4486272.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/744f581b9518fa38e106.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/00e089815401b1153ead.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c091d4a14341565bb0fc.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/995b70e02fb9038c754d.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa036f80967c93666135.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The solution of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa00c111ce008d8bf99d.png\" /> satisfying y(1) = 1 is given by</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a system of parabolas"},{"key":"B","html":"a system of circles"},{"key":"C","html":"y<sup>2</sup> = <em>x</em>(1 + x) – 1"},{"key":"D","html":"(<em>x</em> – 2)<sup>2</sup> + (y – 3)<sup>2</sup> = 5"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/238a378d2f0fec55006d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a system with unity negative feedback is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6f14549b099bd52f9eb9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The value of <em>K</em> for which all the closed-loop poles exist at single point in the s-plane is ___________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[16,16],"answerText":"16","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>16 (16 - 16)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b65fedebd13718e52fe8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19067064ecee8712c82d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6cb19d18877a9ad81fcc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>If the average power delivered to the 5 Ω resistor is 45.24 W then the mutual reactance <em>X<sub>m </sub></em>is __________ Ω. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.5,3.5],"answerText":"2.90","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.90 (2.50 - 3.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2a34fbc96335739e40df.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/46b0a7f974b061f47cd6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the circuit below,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/462daa105bc42795efc7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The MOS transistor serves as an electronic switch. Assume <em>V</em><sub>in</sub> ≈ 0, <em>V<sub>G</sub></em> = 1.8 V, and <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> = 100 Ω. If the circuit is designed to attenuate an incoming small signal by 5%, then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6ab9d05b49de559eeb4a.png\" /> is equal to __________ . (upto two decimal places)<br />\n[Assume V<sub>T</sub> = 0.4 V and μ<sub>n</sub>C<sub>ox</sub> = 200 μA/V<sup>2</sup>]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[660,690],"answerText":"678.57","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>678.57 (660.00 - 690.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/47e239a0b3fe1ff84380.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For a certain transistor, β = 100, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab498242f2db9333416b.png\" />= 1.51 mA and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26e5b9c1d97fac262d0c.png\" /> = 1.515 mA. Then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f710375ec4a17f9844c4.png\" /> is ________ mA. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.95,1.05],"answerText":"1.01","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.01 (0.95 - 1.05)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3b200b751abfb80b805b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f1/f1818a99349b64d9c6ef.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A parabolic reflector antenna is designed to have a directivity of 20 dB at 100 MHz. If the antenna aperture efficiency is 80%, then the required diameter of the antenna will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.71 m"},{"key":"B","html":"3.33 m"},{"key":"C","html":"4.86 m"},{"key":"D","html":"10.67 m"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8c/8c90c2638304d871dab7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the circuit shown below, the switch has been in position ‘a’ for a long time before <em>t</em> = 2 sec. At <em>t</em> = 2 sec, the switch moves instantaneously to position ‘<em>b</em>’. The voltage across capacitor at <em>t</em> = 5 sec will be ____________ V. (upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/081a152a88947963b898.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[14,15],"answerText":"14.84","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>14.84 (14.00 - 15.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/17fd21db8bff0aa9023c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b7c42712478a3863e6f5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the discrete memoryless channel shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bca6f175adb5882042cf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>A decision device is connected at the receiving end of this channel, which makes the decision in favour of <em>m</em><sub>0</sub> when the received symbol is <em>r</em><sub>0</sub> and in favour of <em>m</em><sub>1</sub> when the received symbol is <em>r</em><sub>1</sub>. If this decision device is said to be optimized according to MAP criteria, then the sufficient condition to be satisfied will be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7<em>p</em> + 3<em>q</em> < 7"},{"key":"B","html":"7<em>p</em> + 3<em>q</em> < 3"},{"key":"C","html":"3<em>p</em> + 7<em>q</em> < 7"},{"key":"D","html":"3<em>p</em> + 7<em>q</em> < 3"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f2c5a70f4fb29a49babe.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff9b05c0bbe3af5c8819.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A short circuited stub is connected to a transmission line as shown in the figure below. If Z<sub>0</sub> = 60 Ω, the magnitude of reflection coefficient at the left of the junction of stub and line will be _________.<br />\n(upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b97cd5bd2bf54a4da38c.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.44,0.48],"answerText":"0.46","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.46 (0.44 - 0.48)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1bae178ba61be32b4352.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An abrupt <em>pn</em> junction at <em>T</em> = 300 K and at zero bias has fermi-level in n-side is 4 kT above the intrinsic fermi-level, then the value of donor concentration will be<br />\n(Assume n<sub>i</sub> = 1.5 × 10<sup>10</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.5 × 10<sup>12</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"1.72 × 10<sup>14</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"2.23 × 10<sup>12</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"8.18 × 10<sup>11</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/6506dd73dfc4c8f112ed.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A dielectric interface is defined by 2<sub>x</sub> + 3<em>y</em> = 5 m. The region including the origin is free space where <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0f93a01a25f047f9e772.png\" /> In the other region, ε<sub><em>r</em>2</sub> = 4.2. The electric flux density <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/977ae5c438729d7d0224.png\" /> in this region will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cf/cf71e4b547768c55404c.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/04e57315fbafffc7773d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d64307ad8c51d026550f.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e1fd3a980a407dd79cf1.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/370cbd0177cedf169db3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/267e1ed20cd6cd9ae39f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a closed-loop system with unity negative feedback is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f8436406cab1e5c3ce74.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>It is known that the point “–1 + <em>j</em>0” in <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>)-plane is encircled by the Nyquist plot of the system for two times in counterclockwise direction, then the possible range of the value of <em>K</em> is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0 < <em>K</em> < 0.75"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>K</em> > 0.75"},{"key":"C","html":"0 < <em>K</em> < 0.53"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>K</em> > 0.53"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/773043903466e076a9be.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>When one port of a two port network is open circuited, <em>V</em><sub>1</sub> = 4<em>V</em><sub>2</sub> and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/8859f9012fa5414d095e.png\" /> = 0.25<em>V</em><sub>2</sub>, then which of the<br />\nfollowing is/are correct regarding the two-port parameters?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"z<sub>22</sub> = 4 Ω"},{"key":"B","html":"z<sub>12</sub> = 8 Ω"},{"key":"C","html":"h<sub>12</sub> = 16"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3d/3d60ef902adc8597a8ee.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e8c3c7bfc0cdf2a7ca37.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/98daca71c6fcd6f9915b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For the Bode asymptotic magnitude plot of a minimum phase system shown in figure. The DC gain of the system is ________. (upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/24/243528b8928824ab47c9.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.12,0.13],"answerText":"0.125","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.125 (0.120 - 0.130)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/357f6bdf774e2999c25a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The average power delivered to the impedance <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c367344860ea27b7fc7.png\" /> A is ________ W.</p>\n\n<p>(upto 2 decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[42,44],"answerText":"43.49","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>43.49 (42.00 - 44.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/ca6e811804331f439dce.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9d3091a2f613d9f3aa1a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In what direction from (3, 1, –2), the directional derivative of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f3eb3fd29cf6b587f36.png\" /> is maximum?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c08728a5fe6c811a205.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c9c0b6821c99496248c.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/354926ecf3a0a1593a4a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0ddfc1cc8595074dc6bc.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3fa49effd7ef08311b34.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The eigen values of the following matrix are represented by λ<sub>1</sub> and λ<sub>2</sub></p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a4028cf6adf550d6f92e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ff/ff790bcac7f8f9c0e321.png\" />  is ________. [Correct upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.3,0.35],"answerText":"0.33","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.33 (0.30 - 0.35)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/09da6227d50d915069b2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The value of the integral <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c1d42e35c24045295f2f.png\" /> where c is |z – i| = 1 is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fb88c823165e7c1f8e61.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ee/ee9de08dd19c1057ae3b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f96644904846bc8185d.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cc60ef60dc67fa0196fc.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/12943c097ba89844205f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"MSQ":4,"NAT":26},"withoutKey":0}};
